[Music]  [Applause]  the United Kingdom has one of the  largest and most competitive markets  anywhere in Europe and a man right at  the heart of fibre deployment for a  whole host of providers is Mike Makai  the chairman of open reach Mike thanks  for talking to us today I think before  we start tell us a bit about open region  where it sits in the UK market open  reach was created in 2006 as a result of  a regulatory intervention by Ofcom the  regulator it is the access network  provider in the UK it was separated out  of BT and it was set up to provide  equivalents of products access and so  forth to the access network for a range  of communication provider customers in  the UK now unfortunately the UK doesn't  fit too highly in the ftth council  statistics for Europe what's your  thoughts on and about when we're going  to get full fibre so at the focus that  we've had for the for the last I don't  know how many years has been very much  about solving the digital divide in the  UK making broadband accessible to the  vast majority if not all of the UK homes  and we are now at the position where we  have penetrations in the region of 4050  percent in the UK for superfast we have  coverage of around ninety five percent  as of the end of last year and as a  result of that whilst we still have the  last five percent to fill out which I'm  hoping that the industry will take care  of in their in in the coming few years  we've decided that it's time to build a  network of full fiber optic or fibre to  position us to continue to keep the UK  you know as the largest digital economy  in the g20 and during this time have you  found that your service providers are  being asked for fire but by their own  end-users I think it's a bit early for  that most end-users are quite happy with  the service they get there are many some  of which who are voluble who actually  don't get the service but that is  nothing to do with fiber that's all to  do with how they are currently served  but I think our communication provided  customers today are telling us that we  need to start building a network so that  when the demand is there we are ready to  fulfill it at scale because these these  these cps the likes of sky and talk talk  and indeed bt consumer they think they  need to be able to access a large scale  of population to make the investments  worthwhile on their part to actually  adopt the products so for them to sell  for fiber FTTP as we call it they need  to know that there are a million two  million or whatever it might be  potential homes out there that they can  market to and connect up and of course  there's a wholesaler i need them to be  able to do that because i don't make any  revenue until they connect somebody up  and start paying me for that service ok  Mike thanks very much for talking to us  thank you very much Brian my pleasure so  Openreach a real commitment to full  fiber for the UK  [Music]  [Applause]

